     ssggee — Silicon Integrated Systems SiS190/191 Fast/Gigabit Ethernet driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss
           ddeevviiccee ssggee

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_sge_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssggee device driver provides support for SiS190 Fast Ethernet con‐
     trollers and SiS191 Fast/Gigabit Ethernet controllers.

     All LOMs supported by the ssggee driver have TCP/UDP/IP checksum offload for
     transmit and receive, TCP segmentation offload (TSO), hardware VLAN tag
     stripping/insertion features.  Due to lack of documentation Wake On Lan
     (WOL), Jumbo frame and an interrupt moderation mechanism are not sup‐
     ported yet.

     The ssggee driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                  user can manually override the autoselected mode by adding
                  media options to rc.conf(5).

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Set 10Mbps operation.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX    Set 100Mbps (Fast Ethernet) operation.

     11000000bbaasseeTTXX   Set 1000baseTX operation over twisted pair.

     The ssggee driver supports the following media options:

     ffuullll--dduupplleexx  Force full duplex operation.

     hhaallff--dduupplleexx  Force half duplex operation.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The ssggee device driver provides support for the following Ethernet con‐
     trollers:

     ••   SiS190 Fast Ethernet controller
     ••   SiS191 Fast/Gigabit Ethernet controller

